OL,3,GNEWSAFourth warmest September on record
OL,4,Afor Jersey
OL,5,
OL,6,FJersey has experienced its fourth
OL,7,Fwarmest September on record in 2026,
OL,8,FJersey Met has reported.
OL,10,FIslanders experienced the warmest day
OL,11,Fon 6 September when temperatures hit
OL,12,F28C (82F), which was then followed by
OL,13,Fthe wettest day on 7 September with
OL,14,F10.1mm of rain.
OL,16,FSunshine levels were above average,
OL,17,F215.8 hours of sunshine recorded during
OL,18,Fthe month compared to the 30-year
OL,19,Faverage of 205.7 hours, and the average
OL,20,Ftemperature reached 18.6C (65F)
OL,21,Fcompared to the 30-year average of
OL,22,F16.6C (62F).
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
